NAME=claude-code
VERSION=2.1.112
DESCRIPTION="Claude Code — Anthropic's terminal coding agent (Node cli.js bundle + yoga.wasm TUI)"
CATEGORY=util
# DEPS — node is the runtime; ca-certificates lays down the CA bundle at
# /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt that the /usr/bin/claude launcher points
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS at (so Node's OpenSSL validates api.anthropic.com). Phase
# 90b bring-up: with only DEPS=node, that file was never installed, so the
# launcher referenced a missing path ("Cannot open directory /etc/ssl/certs to
# load OpenSSL certificates") — the solver now auto-installs it dependency-first.
DEPS=node ca-certificates
URL=https://registry.npmjs.org/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/-/claude-code-2.1.112.tgz
SHA256=84379969ea53a0e5fd231a8f77debe4c7cb17dd971f4809d10d33f9aeca5de09
MAINTAINER=m3os

# Phase 90b — Claude Code, the FIRST hosted CLI coding agent on the Phase 85a
# `.m3pkg` substrate. It is delivered the same way every heavy port is: the
# pinned npm registry tarball is fetched + SHA-verified host-side, the package
# payload is staged + sealed into a content-addressed `.m3pkg`, and the offline
# in-OS solver installs it from `/usr/pkg/`. `DEPS=node` makes the solver
# auto-install the Phase 89/90a Node runtime first (the dependency-first proof
# `pkg install tmux`→`libevent` established in 85a). NO live network is needed
# inside the guest to install — see build_claude_code in xtask/src/port_build.rs.
#
# THE PIN — why 2.1.112 and not `latest`. This is a fetch-and-stage port (no
# compiler): the staged payload is the npm package's `cli.js` (a ~9.3 MB minified
# JS bundle) + `yoga.wasm` (the 88 KB WebAssembly TUI layout engine) +
# `vendor/ripgrep/` (the search tool), run under `/usr/bin/node`. **2.1.112 is the
# LAST claude-code version that ships this `cli.js`-under-Node model.** As of
# 2.1.113 the npm package repackaged into a per-platform NATIVE single-file binary
# (a Bun/JavaScriptCore executable, ~500 MB; the wrapper's `install.cjs` copies it
# over a `bin/claude.exe` stub — there is no `cli.js`, and Node is not used at
# all). That native model would invalidate this phase's entire `DEPS=node` +
# Phase 89/90a JIT-Node dependency chain, so the supported pin stays on the last
# Node-runnable release. Running the native Bun binary on m3OS is separate future
# work (a Bun runtime port), not this phase. The Track A spike recorded the
# transition at 2.1.112→2.1.113 and the host `cli.js --version` proof; see
# docs/90b-claude-code.md and docs/roadmap/tasks/90b-claude-code-tasks.md.
#
# RUNTIME — jitless is the first-class default; the JIT node is opt-in for the TUI.
# `claude --version`/`--help`/`-p` run on the Phase 89 JITLESS node (no PKU needed),
# so that is the CI-viable default the M3OS_WITH_CLAUDE block bundles. Claude Code's
# terminal UI additionally instantiates `yoga.wasm` at runtime, which needs the Phase
# 90a JIT `build_node` variant (V8 JIT + WASM under PKU-backed W^X v2); building the
# image with `M3OS_NODE_JIT` set (the gate's `M3OS_CLAUDE_JIT=1` path) bundles that JIT
# node `.m3pkg` instead so the solver resolves `DEPS=node` against the TUI runtime. The
# JIT node runs the real-world cli.js AND renders the interactive `claude` TUI (proven
# by the automated QMP/PPM `claude_tui_render_arm` — the "Welcome to Claude Code
# v2.1.112" onboarding screen paints). The real-world cli.js runs on BOTH variants since
# the Phase 90b W^X-v2 cross-thread PKU read-recovery kernel fix (so cli.js launches).
#
# NOTE — the node build uses `--with-intl=full-icu`, NOT the Phase 89 `small-icu`
# default: Claude Code's TUI calls `Intl.Segmenter.prototype.segment()` for Unicode
# grapheme segmentation (terminal string width / wrapping), which needs ICU's
# break-iterator (`brkitr`) data. small-icu omits that data → the ICU break iterator is
# NULL → V8's `JSSegments::Create` null-dereferences. full-icu (+ `--download=all`)
# compiles the complete ICU data into the binary so the TUI renders.
#
# LAUNCHER — `/usr/bin/claude` (staged by build_claude_code) pins the supported
# environment: NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt (the 86a CA
# bundle, so Node's OpenSSL validates api.anthropic.com), DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1
# (the `.m3pkg` is the only supported delivery), and
# CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1 (no telemetry egress). It is a
# `#!/usr/bin/env node` CJS wrapper that runs cli.js IN-PROCESS via dynamic
# `import()` (single node, no fork) — NOT a `#!/bin/sh` script, because m3OS's
# `/bin/sh` is `ion`, which can't run a shebang script file with flag args.
#
# VENDORED ripgrep — `vendor/ripgrep/x64-linux/rg` is a fully-static `static-pie`
# binary (no PT_INTERP); m3OS's ELF loader handles ET_DYN static-PIE, so it runs
# directly and no separate ripgrep port is needed. The other-platform `rg`
# binaries + the dynamic `audio-capture.node` addon + the `seccomp` helper (m3OS
# has no seccomp) are pruned from the staged tree to keep the artifact lean.
